  "title": "JavaScript Booleans",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "JavaScript Booleans"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "The Boolean Data Type"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "In JavaScript, a Boolean is a primitive data type that can only have one of two values:"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "true or false"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The Boolean value of an expression is the basis for all JavaScript comparisons and\nconditions."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Key Boolean Characteristics"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "true and false are boolean data types",
        "true and false are the only possible boolean values",
        "true and false must be written in lowercase",
        "true and false must be written without quotes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Boolean Use Cases"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Very often, in programming, you will need a data type that can represent one\nof two values, like:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": ["yes or no", "on or off", "true or false"]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Boolean values are fundamental for logical operations and control flow in JavaScript programming."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Comparisons"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "All JavaScript comparison operators (like ==, !=, <, >)\nreturn true or false from the comparison."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Given that x = 5, the table below explains comparison:"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": [],
      "rows": [
        ["Description", "Example", "Returns"],
        ["Equal to", "(x == 8)", "false"],
        ["Not equal to", "(x != 8)", "true"],
        ["Greater than", "(x > 8)", "false"],
        ["Less than", "(x < 8)", "true"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "let x = 5;\n\n(x == 8); // equals false\n\n(x != 8); // equals true",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_boolean_equality"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "See Also:"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "JavaScript Comparisons"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Conditions"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Booleans are extensively used in if statements to determine the code blocks to execute based on the logic."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": [],
      "rows": [
        ["Example", "Result"],
        ["if (day == \"Monday\")", "true or false"],
        ["if (salary > 9000)", "true or false"],
        ["if (age < 18)", "true or false"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "if (hour < 18) {\n\n  greeting = \"Good day\";\n\n} else {\n\n  greeting = \"Good evening\";\n\n}",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_boolean_if"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "See Also:"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "JavaScript if"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "JavaScript if else"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Loops"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Booleans are extensively used in loops to determine conditions for looping."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": [],
      "rows": [
        ["Description", "Example"],
        ["For loop", "for (i = 0; i < 5; i++)"],
        ["While loop", "while (i < 10)"],
        ["For in loop", "for (x in person)"],
        ["For of loop", "for (x of cars)"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "while (i < 10) {\n\n  text += i;\n\n  i++;\n\n}",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_boolean_loop_while"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "See Also:"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "JavaScript Loops"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "The Boolean() Function"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "You can use the Boolean() function to find out if an expression (or a variable) is\ntrue:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "Boolean(10 > 9)",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_boolean_expression1"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Or even easier:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "(10 > 9)",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_boolean_expression2"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Everything With a \"Value\" is True"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "100 is true\n\n3.14 is true\n\n-15 is true\n\ntrue is true\n\n\"Hello\" is true\n\n\"false\" is true\n\n(7 + 1 + 3.14) is true\n\n[ ] is true\n\n{ } is true",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_boolean"
    },
    {
      "type": "h3",
      "text": "Note"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "In JavaScript, both an empty array [ ] and an empty object { } are truthy because they are objects."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "All objects in JavaScript evaluate to true in a boolean context, regardless of their content."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Everything Without a \"Value\" is False"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "0 is false\n\n\"\" is false\n\nundefined is false\n\nnull is false\n\nNaN is false\n\nfalse is false",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "let x = 0;\n\nBoolean(x);",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_boolean_zero"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "let x = -0;\n\nBoolean(x);",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_boolean_minus"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "let x = \"\";\n\nBoolean(x);",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_boolean_empty"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "let x;\n\nBoolean(x);",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_boolean_undefined"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "let x = null;\n\nBoolean(x);",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_boolean_null"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "let x = false;\n\nBoolean(x);",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_boolean_false"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "let x = 10 / \"Hallo\";\n\nBoolean(x);",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_boolean_nan"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "JavaScript Booleans as Objects"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Normally JavaScript booleans are primitive values created from literals:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "let x = false;",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "But booleans can also be defined as objects with the keyword new:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "let y = new Boolean(false);",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "let x = false;\n\nlet y = new Boolean(false);\n\n //\ntypeof x returns boolean\n\n //\ntypeof y returns object",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_booleans_object"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Warning"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Do not create Boolean objects."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The new keyword complicates the code and slows down execution speed."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Boolean objects can produce unexpected results:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "let x = Boolean(false);\n\nlet y = new Boolean(false);\n\n(x == y) returns true\n\n(x === y) returns false",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_booleans_object1"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Comparing two JavaScript objects always returns false."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Complete Boolean Reference"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "For a complete reference, go to our Complete\nJavaScript Boolean Reference."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The reference contains descriptions and examples of all Boolean properties and methods."
    }
  ]
}
